Below is a concise, non-repetitive implementation that adds the multi-page system and Firebase integration for documentation management, building on the existing MarkdownRX integration from the previous turn. It focuses on what’s newly requested: routing/pages, Firestore data model and live CRUD, and Storage-backed image uploads used by the editor. Client components include "use client" as required.

What this adds
- Pages:
  - app/docs/page.tsx: list/search/create
  - app/docs/[slug]/page.tsx: load a single doc and render the Firebase-integrated editor
- Components:
  - components/DocEditor.tsx: loads/saves Firestore docs, integrates uploads to Firebase Storage, and uses MarkdownRXEditor/Preview
- Firestore structure:
  - Collection: docs
  - Doc id: slug (string)
  - Fields: title (string), content (string), tags (string[]), createdAt (timestamp), updatedAt (timestamp)

Assumptions
- lib/firebase exports db (Firestore) and storage (Storage).
- MarkdownRXPreview and MarkdownRXEditor exist as provided earlier (no change needed).
- Tailwind is configured; optional @tailwindcss/typography can be enabled for better preview.

